Z||000000||HF6582||01-03-2000||10:00 PM||||I recieved my pontiac SD4 engine spec book for building differant apps of sd4 engines for racing.  It has all the specs for the pace car motor and several others for drag racing, oval track, road racing and some others.  It also has the manufactors of the various parts used for the build up.  I just wonder how many of them are still making the parts.  The book was printed in 1984, but I bet that most or all of the parts are still available.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||01-03-2000||10:34 PM||||This engine is still used in some racing organizations- Goody's Dash Series. <BR>Available? Yes<BR>Expensive? YES!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||2FAST4U||01-03-2000||11:08 PM||||I know a guy up in Canada that just got out of the road racing business. He has a whole warehouse full of SD4 stuff - from cranks and blocks to complete engines making over 700 HP and fuel injection systems - it 'AINT' cheap but it sure is nice.<P>If your serious about SD4 stuff I'll get his address and phone number for you.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HF6582||01-04-2000||11:26 AM||||If you would get his address I would be greatfull.<P>Thanks <BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000004||SpeedPhreak||01-04-2000||06:50 PM||||get us that info please!  <P>while looking for engine options for my 84 i had it narrowed down to a quad 4 or the v6 out of my moms car & was even considerin a v8 (ive never owned one b4). then i found this site & was all hot & bothered about a 3800 supercharged v6.  then i accidently came across the hot rod '86 online page & fell in love.  dont get me wrong i like bigger engines & actually dont like the idea of a 4 but come on all that reliable streetable power from a 4....that takes care of my need for speed & need for cheap insurance not to mention the sad little looks on all the jap racer fans when they find out what just smoked them.  so im thinking a supercharged sd4!! what do u think.. 350+ hp with the right boost?  n e way the iron duke is coming out this summer & a new sd4 or 3800 is going in.<P>if you put "super duty" in the search engine on this site you'll come across some good threads & a link to kansas racing something or other that is producing NEW & IMPROVED sd4 blocks.  like over 2 grand for the block alone.<P>L8r||||reg||1
Z||000005||David||01-04-2000||07:21 PM||||SpeedPhreak<BR>The name of that company is (was) Kansas Racing Products but they seem to have gone off-line.  Their 4 cyl block was an up-date of the SD4 and it could be custom drilled so that a SBC, SBF, or a Chrysler cylinder head could be used.  You had to specify which drilling that you wanted.  They also had cranks, cams, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000006||HF6582||01-04-2000||10:19 PM||||Kansas Racing Products is back on line.  Really 2 grand is cheap for a racing block, and considering the improvements to the block I think it is a fair price. To build a SD4 it will take some $$$$, but if you want HP it cost money. If you want to spend less money do an engine conversion! This is not for people who want a cheap motor or cheap HP.  You can also modify a stock iron duke into an area to compete with a stock v6, but I wouldn't put my money into a production 4 cylinder you would just get an expensive ticking time bomb (nothing bad against 4 bangger owners I have one).  Now I'm not rich, but I have considered the SD4 for a slow build up project ie ( drive the Iron Duke until she goes while building the SD).<BR>I don't have a scanner, but I would be willing to photo copy the build up sheets and snail mail some one that does if interest is there for it to be posted.<P>Thanks<BR>Scott<P>Just on a side note<BR>I built a 89 mustang that I still have It has a Ford Racing Block in it and the block was over 2grand. It has roughly ten grand in just the motor. It goes really fast in a straight line but that is it.  I would rather be driving my 86GT, 100% a better car.<p>[This message has been edited by HF6582 (edited 01-04-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Monkeyman||01-05-2000||05:23 AM||||I'm not interested in the SD4, but if you want to snailmail the copies I'll scan them and post them or whatever for you.  Email me privately for my address.||||reg||1
Z||000008||2FAST4U||01-06-2000||01:40 AM||||Sorry Guys, I've been so busy the last few days that I almost forgot that I said I'd get the address for the Guy in Canada with all of the SD4 stuff. A lot of the stuff that he has is to sophisitacated for street use like twin cam heads and Lucas 4 port fuel injection but he does have some stuff that can be used in street cars. His name is;<P>Jack Ondrack<BR>Edmonton, Alberta<BR>Phone  (780) 470-0083<BR>Fax    (780) 470-3140<BR>EMAIL   jondrack@telusplanet.net<P>BTW where did you get that SD4 build up book, I'd like to have a copy<p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 01-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||HF6582||01-06-2000||06:21 AM||||Found it at Autolite, they were listed under another book thread. I don't remember the address there.<P>Thanks for the info.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||01-06-2000||10:04 AM||||I too had been intrigued by the SD-4, but if you want 300 HP, SpeedPhreak, there are probably cheaper and more durable options. Pontiac's "streetable" SD-4 made 180-200 hp; the race version made 275-300 hp, but it was NOT a durable engine, with a lot of failures in the valvetrain.  <P>If you look at Fiero racing history, it seemed they always either won or DNF'd.  In fact, the guys I spoke with at Mid-Ohio last fall who were racing an SD-4 Fiero had broken a valve in practice and had to replace the head.||||reg||1
Z||000011||HF6582||01-06-2000||10:48 AM||||Right now I'm in the information gather stage, I have been gathering as much info as I can for the past year.  It is not easy get info on an engine as old as the SD. I'm looking at building one in the 245 HP range. Hopefully one day I build one and put it behind a getrag 5speed, but right now I am still tring to get more info.<BR>If anyone has anything on the motor and you don't mind sharing it I would TIA for any info.<P>Thank You<BR>Scott<p>[This message has been edited by HF6582 (edited 01-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||01-06-2000||12:20 PM||||The 245-275 HP goal is very easily obtained with a SC3800 and I believe it would be a bunch cheaper also. Another benefit is that you will have no trouble with emmisions when it comes to your state and it will soon. Thats my $2(inflation) worth||||reg||1
